1
00:01:34,458 --> 00:01:36,427
I have... no money.

2
00:01:39,296 --> 00:01:40,931
Only 130 yen.

3
00:01:41,131 --> 00:01:44,868
Damn, I thought I had at least a thousand.

4
00:01:45,068 --> 00:01:45,903
Huh...

5
00:01:46,103 --> 00:01:49,940
I have to make 130 yen last a week.

6
00:01:50,407 --> 00:01:53,610
You need to think more before spending your salary.

7
00:01:53,844 --> 00:01:55,879
How many times do I have to tell you, Ryo-chan?

8
00:01:56,213 --> 00:01:57,047
Wait!

9
00:01:58,015 --> 00:01:59,283
I beg you, Reiko-chan.

10
00:01:59,483 --> 00:02:03,487
Just one bowl of katsudon, then I'll only have water till the end of the month!

11
00:02:03,887 --> 00:02:04,721
No way!

12
00:02:05,622 --> 00:02:09,393
Why don't you learn from this and use an expense tracker next month?

13
00:02:10,294 --> 00:02:14,298
Damn it! You could at least lend me a little!

14
00:02:15,933 --> 00:02:17,601
I'm starving...

15
00:02:18,635 --> 00:02:20,938
But there's nothing to eat.

16
00:02:21,138 --> 00:02:22,406
I'll watch TV.

17
00:02:24,908 --> 00:02:27,311
&lt;i&gt;This meat is so juicy!&lt;/i&gt;

18
00:02:31,281 --> 00:02:32,349
&lt;i&gt;It's delicious!&lt;/i&gt;

19
00:02:33,717 --> 00:02:36,920
&lt;i&gt;It's so tender and melts in my mouth!&lt;/i&gt;

20
00:02:37,121 --> 00:02:41,625
-Damn! Eating meat before payday! &lt;i&gt;-This is the best! I can't resist!&lt;/i&gt;

21
00:02:41,825 --> 00:02:43,827
Don't air such a show!

22
00:02:45,129 --> 00:02:47,264
&lt;i&gt;I love you.&lt;/i&gt;

23
00:02:47,731 --> 00:02:50,667
&lt;i&gt;I really love you.&lt;/i&gt;

24
00:02:50,901 --> 00:02:52,002
&lt;i&gt;I really, really...&lt;/i&gt;

25
00:02:52,202 --> 00:02:53,904
&lt;i&gt;I really, really love you.&lt;/i&gt;

26
00:02:54,138 --> 00:02:55,506
-Gah! &lt;i&gt;-I really, really love you.&lt;/i&gt;

27
00:02:55,739 --> 00:02:59,510
It's because you make stuff like this that you only get 3% viewership!

28
00:02:59,743 --> 00:03:00,978
Oh, Ryo-chan.

29
00:03:01,445 --> 00:03:04,081
You seem to know a lot about TV ratings.

30
00:03:04,281 --> 00:03:08,185
-It's common knowledge these days. -Yeah, yeah.

31
00:03:10,087 --> 00:03:14,091
&lt;i&gt;Mimi-chan gets shampooed&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;at a dog salon every week.&lt;/i&gt;

32
00:03:14,291 --> 00:03:15,526
&lt;i&gt;Her clothes are from Hyanel.&lt;/i&gt;

33
00:03:15,759 --> 00:03:17,628
&lt;i&gt;Her shoes are custom-made&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;by Herragamo.&lt;/i&gt;

34
00:03:17,828 --> 00:03:19,930
&lt;i&gt;Kobe beef is her favorite food.&lt;/i&gt;

35
00:03:21,565 --> 00:03:24,368
Argh! She's just a dog!

36
00:03:30,674 --> 00:03:32,576
What's Ryo-san doing?

37
00:03:32,809 --> 00:03:35,779
Maybe he's hungry and hallucinating.

38
00:03:36,513 --> 00:03:38,315
-Let's eat quickly! -Yeah.

39
00:03:39,216 --> 00:03:40,384
Damn it!

40
00:03:43,887 --> 00:03:47,991
TV these days doesn't understand the feeling of its viewers at all!

41
00:03:48,192 --> 00:03:51,028
Gah, it's so annoying!

42
00:03:53,163 --> 00:03:55,866
Oh, those are bowls of katsudon from Tsurukame-ken!

43
00:03:56,266 --> 00:04:00,203
And you've saved one for me too, Reiko?

44
00:04:02,206 --> 00:04:03,507
This is for Kei-chan!

45
00:04:03,707 --> 00:04:05,709
Aw, don't be so uptight.

46
00:04:06,743 --> 00:04:09,079
I said it's Kei-chan's!

47
00:04:09,279 --> 00:04:11,515
By the way, Nakagawa is late.

48
00:04:11,715 --> 00:04:15,819
Oh, you're right. It's about time he came back from patrol.

49
00:04:16,019 --> 00:04:19,756
&lt;i&gt;When Tsurukame-ken's katsudon&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;gets cold, it loses half its flavor.&lt;/i&gt;

50
00:04:20,190 --> 00:04:21,058
I'll eat it!

51
00:04:23,026 --> 00:04:23,860
Ryo-chan!

52
00:04:24,461 --> 00:04:27,431
If you eat someone's food without permission, it's theft!

53
00:04:28,232 --> 00:04:30,634
I-I-I don't care!

54
00:04:31,768 --> 00:04:33,370
Ryo-chan!

55
00:04:38,475 --> 00:04:42,079
Reiko is so stingy. I didn't even get a bite.

56
00:04:43,914 --> 00:04:47,050
-Ouch! -What are you doing? We'll miss Nakarin!

57
00:04:47,251 --> 00:04:48,785
Watch it, old man!

58
00:04:49,186 --> 00:04:50,721
O-Old man?

59
00:04:50,921 --> 00:04:54,858
-Nakagawa-san! -You're so cool!

60
00:04:55,058 --> 00:04:56,493
W-What the heck's going on?

61
00:04:56,727 --> 00:05:00,297
-You're so handsome, Nakagawa-san! -Give me an autograph!

62
00:05:00,797 --> 00:05:03,100
Sorry, I'm on duty now.

63
00:05:03,300 --> 00:05:05,102
Please make way!

64
00:05:05,302 --> 00:05:08,238
-Nakarin, look this way! -Nakarin?

65
00:05:08,438 --> 00:05:09,406
Out of the way!

66
00:05:09,740 --> 00:05:10,874
R-Ryotsu!

67
00:05:11,074 --> 00:05:14,144
Oh, it's you, Nakagawa. What are you doing here?

68
00:05:14,344 --> 00:05:16,513
Ryotsu, please help me!

69
00:05:16,747 --> 00:05:18,915
What's all this fuss about?

70
00:05:19,116 --> 00:05:19,983
I don't know.

71
00:05:21,885 --> 00:05:23,954
Are you all right, Ryotsu?

72
00:05:27,424 --> 00:05:30,927
N-Nakagawa, do something!

73
00:05:31,128 --> 00:05:33,797
I-I can't move forward one centimeter like this!

74
00:05:33,997 --> 00:05:36,667
I'll help you if you let me eat your katsudon!

75
00:05:36,900 --> 00:05:37,901
Yes, please!

76
00:05:38,101 --> 00:05:38,935
All right!

77
00:05:41,605 --> 00:05:45,509
Move, move! Step aside!

78
00:05:45,709 --> 00:05:46,943
Get out of the way!

79
00:05:48,545 --> 00:05:50,614
-Move, old man! -Shut up!

80
00:05:53,850 --> 00:05:56,119
-Now's your chance, Nakagawa! -Okay!

81
00:05:57,154 --> 00:05:59,656
Ahh! He's so cool!

82
00:06:01,692 --> 00:06:04,094
-Nakagawa-san! -Nakarin!

83
00:06:04,695 --> 00:06:06,863
Well, I'm sure glad you came.

84
00:06:07,097 --> 00:06:08,965
Just put me down now!

85
00:06:09,399 --> 00:06:10,701
Got it. Oh!

86
00:06:18,041 --> 00:06:20,510
Ryotsu! Are you okay?

87
00:06:21,345 --> 00:06:22,579
If you're gonna stop, say so!

88
00:06:22,813 --> 00:06:24,648
Sorry, that microbus suddenly...

89
00:06:24,848 --> 00:06:26,016
Excuse me...

90
00:06:27,551 --> 00:06:31,688
I'm Sugihara, a producer at Kanto Television.

91
00:06:32,355 --> 00:06:33,390
Kanto Television?

92
00:06:34,691 --> 00:06:37,761
And I'm Yamamoto, a director!

93
00:06:38,195 --> 00:06:40,897
So, what business does Kanto TV have with us?

94
00:06:41,131 --> 00:06:42,899
Well, you see...

95
00:06:43,133 --> 00:06:47,704
I'll get straight to the point. "A Day in the Life of Officer Nakagawa"!

96
00:06:48,238 --> 00:06:49,072
Okay?

97
00:06:49,306 --> 00:06:51,575
"&lt;i&gt;24-Hour Close-Up&lt;/i&gt;"?

98
00:06:51,908 --> 00:06:52,743
Oh!

99
00:06:55,045 --> 00:06:57,147
Um... why me?

100
00:06:57,681 --> 00:06:59,082
Look at this.

101
00:06:59,516 --> 00:07:01,051
Oh, it's you!

102
00:07:01,451 --> 00:07:03,887
In the "Cool Guys Spotted Around Town" Contest,

103
00:07:04,087 --> 00:07:06,923
you were the clear winner!

104
00:07:07,224 --> 00:07:09,626
This is the reason for the fuss earlier.

105
00:07:10,193 --> 00:07:11,027
Ah!

106
00:07:15,432 --> 00:07:16,767
Hello?

107
00:07:17,234 --> 00:07:19,936
&lt;i&gt;Nakagawa, have you met&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;the Kanto TV staff?&lt;/i&gt;

108
00:07:20,170 --> 00:07:23,573
Yes, but Chief, what does it mean?

109
00:07:23,774 --> 00:07:28,345
If you appear on TV, it'll improve the image of Katsushika PD.

110
00:07:28,545 --> 00:07:30,080
Please cooperate with them.

111
00:07:30,280 --> 00:07:31,782
Wait, Chief!

112
00:07:32,382 --> 00:07:34,818
-Ah! -Nakarin!

113
00:07:35,185 --> 00:07:36,620
Look! Here they come again!

114
00:07:36,820 --> 00:07:38,388
Nakagawa, do something!

115
00:07:38,588 --> 00:07:40,490
You want to film my entire day, right?

116
00:07:40,724 --> 00:07:41,558
Yes!

117
00:07:41,758 --> 00:07:43,026
Okay, let's do it!

118
00:07:43,226 --> 00:07:44,561
Great!

119
00:07:44,761 --> 00:07:46,229
Follow me, then!

120
00:07:46,430 --> 00:07:47,297
Okay!

121
00:08:00,944 --> 00:08:03,146
It's morning, young master.

122
00:08:03,380 --> 00:08:05,148
Oh, good morning.

123
00:08:17,260 --> 00:08:20,964
The Burberry uniforms you ordered have arrived from England.

124
00:08:21,164 --> 00:08:23,533
Yeah, I'll try them on when I get back.

125
00:08:31,775 --> 00:08:34,344
Have a nice day, young master.

126
00:08:37,547 --> 00:08:38,648
Cut!

127
00:08:38,849 --> 00:08:42,652
Whew, okay! That was great, Nakagawa-chan!

128
00:08:42,853 --> 00:08:45,989
I tried to recreate the atmosphere of this morning.

129
00:08:46,423 --> 00:08:50,293
Well, I'm sure we'll get a 20% audience share with this!

130
00:08:50,493 --> 00:08:53,897
-You have no idea how viewers feel. -What?

131
00:08:54,297 --> 00:08:56,132
&lt;i&gt;24-Hour Close-Up&lt;/i&gt;

132
00:08:56,333 --> 00:09:00,704
has recently been consistently competing for the worst ratings.

133
00:09:00,904 --> 00:09:04,107
1.2%, 1.0%, and 1.3%.

134
00:09:04,441 --> 00:09:07,811
-At this rate, it'll be canceled for sure! -Gasp!

135
00:09:08,011 --> 00:09:10,914
What do you know, amateur!

136
00:09:11,147 --> 00:09:13,183
The viewers are amateurs too!

137
00:09:14,518 --> 00:09:19,155
A few years ago, the show covered an old man's food stall.

138
00:09:19,356 --> 00:09:22,759
It must have hit an audience share of 20%!

139
00:09:22,993 --> 00:09:24,861
The emotion of that moment.

140
00:09:25,061 --> 00:09:27,197
The old man's smile.

141
00:09:27,731 --> 00:09:30,600
Those are still burned into my mind.

142
00:09:31,535 --> 00:09:32,602
Ohhh!

143
00:09:33,169 --> 00:09:35,605
&lt;i&gt;24-Hour Close-Up&lt;/i&gt; was popular

144
00:09:36,006 --> 00:09:39,042
because it humbly yet lovingly depicted ordinary people's lives.

145
00:09:39,242 --> 00:09:43,313
It was once regarded as the very conscience of Kanto TV.

146
00:09:43,613 --> 00:09:44,781
But look at it now!

147
00:09:45,315 --> 00:09:49,319
Just showing Nakagawa's wealth as it is, and calling it okay?

148
00:09:49,519 --> 00:09:52,022
We can't keep doing the same thing forever!

149
00:09:52,622 --> 00:09:54,257
Hmph! Aren't you professionals?

150
00:09:54,491 --> 00:09:56,493
"RAMEN"

151
00:09:56,693 --> 00:09:58,428
Hey! Ramen and some dumplings!

152
00:09:58,628 --> 00:09:59,496
Hmm?

153
00:10:01,631 --> 00:10:04,267
-Welcome. -Do you understand?

154
00:10:04,501 --> 00:10:07,938
To the customer who just walked into a ramen restaurant,

155
00:10:08,171 --> 00:10:10,941
you're trying to serve spaghetti!

156
00:10:12,409 --> 00:10:13,443
That's right!

157
00:10:14,110 --> 00:10:15,245
You're absolutely right!

158
00:10:15,445 --> 00:10:17,113
S-Sugihara-chan!

159
00:10:17,781 --> 00:10:22,085
What kind of shows do viewers want right now?

160
00:10:22,285 --> 00:10:23,186
H-Hey...

161
00:10:23,386 --> 00:10:27,824
For example, those tear-jerking reunion shows.

162
00:10:28,124 --> 00:10:33,129
They're nothing but misery-peeping contests in the name of "reunion."

163
00:10:33,363 --> 00:10:34,598
What do you mean?

164
00:10:35,098 --> 00:10:35,932
Listen.

165
00:10:36,132 --> 00:10:39,202
Viewers want to see other people being unhappy.

166
00:10:39,402 --> 00:10:42,005
Fulfill that desire.

167
00:10:42,238 --> 00:10:43,840
The project's concept is...

168
00:10:44,074 --> 00:10:45,742
"POVERTY"

169
00:10:45,942 --> 00:10:47,677
Poverty!

170
00:10:47,911 --> 00:10:49,112
I see!

171
00:10:50,981 --> 00:10:54,250
Depending on negotiations, this high-ratings contractor

172
00:10:54,451 --> 00:10:58,488
known as genius director Ryotsu-sama might just step in and go the extra mile!

173
00:10:58,788 --> 00:11:01,491
-Let's give it a shot. -But...!

174
00:11:02,292 --> 00:11:05,028
Please lend us your wisdom, Director Ryotsu!

175
00:11:05,261 --> 00:11:07,564
100,000 yen per ratings point.

176
00:11:07,764 --> 00:11:09,799
That's my commission.

177
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:12,402
100,000 yen per ratings point?!

178
00:11:12,802 --> 00:11:15,839
What on earth is Ryotsu thinking?

179
00:11:17,040 --> 00:11:21,344
&lt;i&gt;My grand plan to turn Nakagawa-chan&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;into a complete commoner!&lt;/i&gt;

180
00:11:21,845 --> 00:11:23,813
Action!

181
00:11:35,592 --> 00:11:37,861
We'll say Nakagawa lives in this dorm.

182
00:11:38,795 --> 00:11:42,065
A cheerful and modest life in a dorm for single men.

183
00:11:42,699 --> 00:11:44,034
You know, Ryotsu-chan.

184
00:11:44,834 --> 00:11:46,636
I think faking it is a bad idea.

185
00:11:46,970 --> 00:11:47,804
Faking?

186
00:11:48,271 --> 00:11:49,305
What did you say?

187
00:11:49,606 --> 00:11:51,741
This is not faking!

188
00:11:51,975 --> 00:11:53,977
Then, what is it?

189
00:11:54,844 --> 00:11:55,712
It's staging.

190
00:11:56,379 --> 00:11:58,214
Staging, huh...

191
00:12:01,217 --> 00:12:03,620
Hey, I'm back.

192
00:12:03,987 --> 00:12:06,856
-Oh, Ryo-san, you're home early. -Yeah, I guess so.

193
00:12:07,057 --> 00:12:08,858
Don't be shy, come in.

194
00:12:09,059 --> 00:12:10,026
Oh, you have guests?

195
00:12:10,226 --> 00:12:12,095
I'll put you on TV, too.

196
00:12:12,328 --> 00:12:13,663
What? TV?

197
00:12:13,863 --> 00:12:17,067
Thank you. Sorry for barging in when you're busy.

198
00:12:17,300 --> 00:12:18,168
Oh my...

199
00:12:29,779 --> 00:12:30,880
Th-This is awful.

200
00:12:31,247 --> 00:12:36,553
M-Maybe this place would make the viewers feel superior, but still...

201
00:12:38,555 --> 00:12:42,058
Um, do you really live here?

202
00:12:42,258 --> 00:12:43,493
Of course I do!

203
00:12:44,794 --> 00:12:47,864
Come on in, don't be shy. I'll make you some tea.

204
00:12:48,531 --> 00:12:49,599
No, thanks!

205
00:12:51,367 --> 00:12:53,269
Hmm, let's start with the waking-up shot.

206
00:12:53,803 --> 00:12:55,271
Aim here from a low position,

207
00:12:55,705 --> 00:12:57,273
and then pan up.

208
00:12:57,774 --> 00:12:59,776
Twist the shot from above his head,

209
00:13:00,810 --> 00:13:02,245
and zoom right in on his face!

210
00:13:02,445 --> 00:13:05,048
Huh! This is why amateurs are so annoying.

211
00:13:05,348 --> 00:13:07,984
Such unnatural camera work is a total no-no!

212
00:13:08,618 --> 00:13:09,819
Right, Sugihara-chan?

213
00:13:10,053 --> 00:13:11,521
Y-Yeah...

214
00:13:11,821 --> 00:13:14,224
Shut up, low-ratings director!

215
00:13:14,424 --> 00:13:15,391
What?

216
00:13:15,592 --> 00:13:19,629
Even a fresh fish is unlucky if it ends up with a bad chef.

217
00:13:20,797 --> 00:13:22,799
All right, let's see!

218
00:13:24,534 --> 00:13:27,570
Um, do I have to sleep on this futon?

219
00:13:27,770 --> 00:13:29,939
You can't sleep in your uniform.

220
00:13:30,140 --> 00:13:31,641
Hurry up and take off your jacket!

221
00:13:31,975 --> 00:13:34,310
Oh, um... where are my pajamas?

222
00:13:34,544 --> 00:13:37,614
Pajamas? Oh well, if you insist...

223
00:13:38,181 --> 00:13:40,383
I'm sure there are some in here...

224
00:13:43,019 --> 00:13:44,420
Well, anyway,

225
00:13:44,621 --> 00:13:47,490
the common cop stands by in his own shirt.

226
00:13:49,626 --> 00:13:51,027
Like this?

227
00:13:51,261 --> 00:13:53,663
Hmm, something's wrong.

228
00:13:53,863 --> 00:13:54,797
Hey, AD!

229
00:13:54,998 --> 00:13:55,999
Huh?

230
00:13:56,566 --> 00:13:58,735
-I mean you. -Me?

231
00:13:59,335 --> 00:14:00,336
What?

232
00:14:00,570 --> 00:14:02,972
Yamamoto-chan, hold it together for now.

233
00:14:03,173 --> 00:14:04,774
Yes, what is it?

234
00:14:04,974 --> 00:14:07,277
Move that over there, and that over there.

235
00:14:07,477 --> 00:14:09,312
Swap this and that around.

236
00:14:09,512 --> 00:14:10,346
Okay.

237
00:14:15,318 --> 00:14:18,988
No, no! It's not enough to just line them up!

238
00:14:19,189 --> 00:14:20,857
Here! Like this!

239
00:14:21,057 --> 00:14:23,793
-Hey, Nakagawa. Reach out your hand. -Oh, okay...

240
00:14:27,430 --> 00:14:29,699
Everything is within reach!

241
00:14:30,033 --> 00:14:32,368
Then, casually put a picture of a beautiful woman.

242
00:14:36,472 --> 00:14:39,142
This is what you call realism.

243
00:14:39,509 --> 00:14:41,044
By the way, AD Yamamoto?

244
00:14:41,811 --> 00:14:42,779
Ah, yes!

245
00:14:42,979 --> 00:14:45,715
-Don't you think something is missing? -What?

246
00:14:46,049 --> 00:14:49,185
What a pathetic guy! You really don't get it?

247
00:14:49,385 --> 00:14:50,854
How should I know?

248
00:14:51,487 --> 00:14:52,555
A mosquito repellent pig.

249
00:14:54,157 --> 00:14:55,358
A mosquito repellent pig?

250
00:14:57,026 --> 00:14:59,028
Go and buy one right now. Get a move on!

251
00:14:59,229 --> 00:15:01,064
Fine, I'll go get one!

252
00:15:01,397 --> 00:15:03,733
A mosquito repellent pig in winter, Ryotsu?

253
00:15:04,267 --> 00:15:06,236
Nakagawa, you won't get it.

254
00:15:06,836 --> 00:15:08,905
A summer wind chime by the winter window.

255
00:15:09,405 --> 00:15:11,708
A winter kotatsu as a midsummer dining table.

256
00:15:11,941 --> 00:15:14,677
That's the melancholy of a single man.

257
00:15:15,078 --> 00:15:18,047
This will squeeze out the tears of housewives.

258
00:15:18,248 --> 00:15:19,849
But, faking is...

259
00:15:20,049 --> 00:15:24,187
I think the audience share will easily go up by 3%.

260
00:15:24,387 --> 00:15:25,421
As you wish!

261
00:15:25,655 --> 00:15:26,589
"SHAVED ICE"

262
00:15:28,925 --> 00:15:32,028
Whew! I can really feel the melancholy.

263
00:15:32,228 --> 00:15:33,863
Standby, okay!

264
00:15:39,302 --> 00:15:40,937
Ah, I slept well.

265
00:15:41,738 --> 00:15:43,106
It's fine weather, too.

266
00:15:43,306 --> 00:15:44,307
Cut!

267
00:15:44,908 --> 00:15:45,875
Eh, why?

268
00:15:46,075 --> 00:15:48,978
No commoner has such a perfect face when they wake up!

269
00:15:51,514 --> 00:15:52,782
Argh!

270
00:15:53,216 --> 00:15:55,551
No stylish setting lotion here.

271
00:15:55,752 --> 00:15:58,855
Leftover oil from the frying pan will give you a bedhead.

272
00:15:59,055 --> 00:16:03,726
Red eyes and a little puffiness after a nightcap and staying up late!

273
00:16:04,294 --> 00:16:06,062
Not puffy enough?

274
00:16:06,329 --> 00:16:09,465
Um, Ryotsu-chan, I think that's enough.

275
00:16:11,768 --> 00:16:14,270
-Stay outta my staging! -Eeek!

276
00:16:15,171 --> 00:16:17,774
The finishing touch is some just-woken-up clothes.

277
00:16:17,974 --> 00:16:19,542
Due to budget constraints...

278
00:16:20,243 --> 00:16:21,277
Whoa!

279
00:16:21,477 --> 00:16:23,646
N-No more, please!

280
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:26,983
This is part of the job, Nakagawa!

281
00:16:27,183 --> 00:16:29,819
All right! It's getting realistic!

282
00:16:31,287 --> 00:16:33,656
Watch carefully! I'm only gonna do this once.

283
00:16:33,890 --> 00:16:34,657
Okay!

284
00:16:36,893 --> 00:16:38,928
-Damn alarm! -Eeek!

285
00:16:43,132 --> 00:16:44,634
Good morning!

286
00:16:44,834 --> 00:16:47,637
A wake-up kiss!

287
00:16:48,838 --> 00:16:49,672
Huh?

288
00:16:50,306 --> 00:16:53,576
See that? This is what people do when they wake up!

289
00:16:53,776 --> 00:16:55,445
-Try it yourself! -O-Okay!

290
00:17:03,653 --> 00:17:05,154
No! All wrong!

291
00:17:07,757 --> 00:17:13,296
You're still wondering why a handsome, rich guy like you has to do this.

292
00:17:13,496 --> 00:17:15,164
Aren't you?

293
00:17:15,365 --> 00:17:16,699
N-No, I'm not!

294
00:17:17,066 --> 00:17:21,537
"After all, I live on a different level from commoners, baby."

295
00:17:21,838 --> 00:17:24,640
I can see that obnoxious pride coming through!

296
00:17:25,007 --> 00:17:27,877
-That's not what I'm— -Throw away all your pride!

297
00:17:28,344 --> 00:17:30,813
Your status as the heir to the Nakagawa Corporation.

298
00:17:31,014 --> 00:17:32,982
Your pride as a handsome man.

299
00:17:33,483 --> 00:17:36,152
Throw it all away and strip naked!

300
00:17:36,352 --> 00:17:37,553
He's tough.

301
00:17:37,820 --> 00:17:39,155
I... I lost.

302
00:17:42,992 --> 00:17:44,193
Good morning.

303
00:17:44,394 --> 00:17:46,396
A wake-up kiss!

304
00:17:51,801 --> 00:17:53,436
It's cold again this morning!

305
00:17:55,438 --> 00:17:56,672
Damn it!

306
00:18:00,843 --> 00:18:03,246
Ahh! It stinks!

307
00:18:03,746 --> 00:18:07,350
Wow, what? There's mold on this one!

308
00:18:07,550 --> 00:18:08,684
Oh, this one is...

309
00:18:12,055 --> 00:18:15,458
I wiped up with this after eating noodles some time ago.

310
00:18:15,691 --> 00:18:17,860
It must've been growing since then!

311
00:18:18,461 --> 00:18:20,997
Well, at least for another week or two...

312
00:18:22,031 --> 00:18:24,934
Oh! I can just use it like this.

313
00:18:30,907 --> 00:18:32,742
Sorry, Ryotsu...

314
00:18:32,942 --> 00:18:34,043
I can't fart.

315
00:18:34,677 --> 00:18:36,746
Cut! That's okay!

316
00:18:37,447 --> 00:18:39,549
Well, that final fart aside,

317
00:18:40,783 --> 00:18:43,252
you've really moved on as a person, Nakagawa.

318
00:18:43,453 --> 00:18:46,622
-I'm sure we'll get a viewership of 5%! -Oh...

319
00:18:46,856 --> 00:18:51,461
Now, it's all about cramming in as much crowd-pleasing stuff as we can!

320
00:18:59,435 --> 00:19:01,938
Poor common cop Nakagawa-kun

321
00:19:02,138 --> 00:19:05,475
even scavenges garbage cans to save on food expenses.

322
00:19:05,942 --> 00:19:06,742
But then...!

323
00:19:08,611 --> 00:19:09,445
Here you are.

324
00:19:10,313 --> 00:19:16,652
Kind Nakagawa-kun shares the fried chicken bento he scavenged for dinner with a dog.

325
00:19:18,821 --> 00:19:24,293
This will win the hearts of dog lovers and increase the audience share by 1%!

326
00:19:24,494 --> 00:19:26,262
-Yay! -Wow!

327
00:19:26,462 --> 00:19:31,167
Nakagawa-kun is also a brotherly cop who loves children.

328
00:19:31,367 --> 00:19:36,439
This will delight housewives and kids, pushing up the ratings by 1%!

329
00:19:36,639 --> 00:19:38,841
"RAMEN RESTAURANT FUKUKAME-TEI"

330
00:19:40,376 --> 00:19:45,448
At Kameari Park Police Station, there's the respectable Officer Ryotsu,

331
00:19:45,915 --> 00:19:50,853
who sometimes treats hungry Nakagawa-kun to noodles.

332
00:19:51,487 --> 00:19:56,859
Showing noodles that impress even gourmets will boost the ratings by 10%!

333
00:19:59,562 --> 00:20:01,631
What's going on, Ryo-chan?

334
00:20:01,831 --> 00:20:06,369
No! The camera's too high! I'll film it!

335
00:20:10,673 --> 00:20:13,643
Okay, Reiko, just keep walking straight.

336
00:20:13,843 --> 00:20:17,713
Stop it! Don't film from too low, okay?

337
00:20:18,881 --> 00:20:21,984
And then, Nakagawa comes into the frame. Rain!

338
00:20:22,185 --> 00:20:23,519
Sure!

339
00:20:26,489 --> 00:20:29,258
A sexy beauty and a handsome guy in unrequited love...

340
00:20:30,393 --> 00:20:32,028
What percentage will this get?

341
00:20:32,228 --> 00:20:35,231
Capturing daytime soap opera fans will boost viewership by 5%.

342
00:20:35,665 --> 00:20:37,733
-What time is it now? -It's 4:30.

343
00:20:37,967 --> 00:20:39,235
Okay, she's be here soon!

344
00:20:41,837 --> 00:20:44,440
Oh, that's the lady from Nikoniko Dormitory.

345
00:20:44,974 --> 00:20:46,576
Go, Nakagawa!

346
00:20:52,148 --> 00:20:53,416
Oh, what's going on?

347
00:20:53,616 --> 00:20:55,551
Mom!

348
00:20:56,152 --> 00:20:57,153
You're my mom, right?

349
00:20:57,553 --> 00:21:00,890
-It's me, Keiichi! -What are you talking about?

350
00:21:01,090 --> 00:21:03,626
I don't remember giving birth to you!

351
00:21:04,927 --> 00:21:07,997
I missed you, Mom!

352
00:21:08,631 --> 00:21:10,733
Ryo-san, what are you doing there?

353
00:21:10,933 --> 00:21:12,401
Director, could it be...

354
00:21:12,835 --> 00:21:14,704
I didn't tell her about it.

355
00:21:14,904 --> 00:21:17,440
With amateurs, it's all about getting natural reactions!

356
00:21:17,907 --> 00:21:21,110
-I missed you! -We'll dub her lines later.

357
00:21:21,944 --> 00:21:24,213
What percentage will the reunion with his mom get?

358
00:21:24,413 --> 00:21:27,450
Another 18% for the tears and emotions!

359
00:21:27,650 --> 00:21:30,620
That means a total audience share of 40%,

360
00:21:30,853 --> 00:21:33,956
which multiplied by 100,000 equals four million yen!

361
00:21:34,190 --> 00:21:37,460
-What are you doing? -Now, Nakagawa-kun, lost in tears,

362
00:21:39,495 --> 00:21:41,230
goes into a public bath.

363
00:21:42,898 --> 00:21:43,733
Ah!

364
00:21:44,967 --> 00:21:48,337
Mischievous Nakagawa-kun sometimes enters the women's bath by mistake.

365
00:21:48,571 --> 00:21:50,473
Um, soap, soap...

366
00:21:50,906 --> 00:21:51,741
Oh!

367
00:21:52,108 --> 00:21:53,976
I found it! Huh?

368
00:21:54,644 --> 00:21:56,245
Shampoo!

369
00:21:57,880 --> 00:21:59,148
Lucky! There's some left.

370
00:21:59,448 --> 00:22:03,819
The common cop collects and uses discarded soap and shampoo.

371
00:22:04,053 --> 00:22:05,488
"FRUIT MILK"

372
00:22:05,688 --> 00:22:08,424
And finally, he wraps it up with some classic fruit milk.

373
00:22:08,891 --> 00:22:10,660
Right, the climax!

374
00:22:10,960 --> 00:22:15,331
&lt;i&gt;And so, common police officer&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Nakagawa-kun's day comes to an end.&lt;/i&gt;

375
00:22:15,665 --> 00:22:18,834
&lt;i&gt;-Mom!&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;-Keiichi, Keiichi...&lt;/i&gt;

376
00:22:19,068 --> 00:22:21,337
&lt;i&gt;-I missed you!&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;-I missed you, too!&lt;/i&gt;

377
00:22:22,371 --> 00:22:26,442
&lt;i&gt;Reiko-san!&lt;/i&gt;

378
00:22:27,343 --> 00:22:30,346
&lt;i&gt;"PRODUCER&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;AKIO SUGIHARA"&lt;/i&gt;

379
00:22:32,248 --> 00:22:34,016
Well done, Nakagawa!

380
00:22:34,550 --> 00:22:37,186
You truly acted like a commoner!

381
00:22:38,321 --> 00:22:41,624
That's too much. Poor Kei-chan.

382
00:22:41,991 --> 00:22:43,693
That was someone else...

383
00:22:43,926 --> 00:22:45,528
It wasn't me!

384
00:22:45,961 --> 00:22:48,297
Nakagawa-chan! Ryotsu-chan!

385
00:22:48,497 --> 00:22:49,932
"GOOD LUCK, NAKAGAWA-KUN!"

386
00:22:50,466 --> 00:22:51,534
So...

387
00:22:52,101 --> 00:22:56,339
Right after the show aired, letters of encouragement, faxes and packages

388
00:22:56,539 --> 00:23:00,142
filled the staff room, all sent to Nakagawa-chan from across the country.

389
00:23:00,710 --> 00:23:03,412
It's all thanks to Nakagawa's great performance.

390
00:23:03,646 --> 00:23:06,482
I've fooled the public.

391
00:23:06,682 --> 00:23:09,385
-How should I apologize? -Oh, yes!

392
00:23:09,819 --> 00:23:12,688
By the way, what were the ratings?

393
00:23:13,155 --> 00:23:14,690
A whopping 30%!

394
00:23:14,990 --> 00:23:16,759
Oh! That means...

395
00:23:16,992 --> 00:23:19,061
One, two, three...

396
00:23:19,295 --> 00:23:21,330
My share is three million!

397
00:23:21,864 --> 00:23:26,769
But the station found out that you were the director...

398
00:23:27,002 --> 00:23:29,705
They don't want anyone less capable than an amateur.

399
00:23:29,905 --> 00:23:31,540
-So we both got... -fired!

400
00:23:31,741 --> 00:23:33,542
So, there's no money!

401
00:23:33,743 --> 00:23:35,511
W-What?!

402
00:23:35,711 --> 00:23:36,579
-Ryotsu! -Uh-oh.

403
00:23:38,381 --> 00:23:39,749
Ch-Chief!

404
00:23:39,982 --> 00:23:43,686
So that phony show was your work after all!

405
00:23:43,886 --> 00:23:47,523
Th-That was the blood, sweat, and tears of me and Nakagawa!

406
00:23:47,723 --> 00:23:48,557
Right?

407
00:23:49,091 --> 00:23:51,026
Because Ryotsu forced me to do it!

408
00:23:51,694 --> 00:23:53,696
Chief, it was pretty good, wasn't it?

409
00:23:53,896 --> 00:23:56,532
How could you...!

410
00:23:56,732 --> 00:23:59,635
You idiot!

411
00:24:03,005 --> 00:24:08,844
NEPO BABY REIJI SHIRATORI
